            <ArticleTitle>Occult coronary ostial obstruction late after arterial switch operation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>308-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/jocs.12083</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Occult coronary artery obstruction can be a late source of morbidity and mortality following the arterial switch operation for transposition of the great arteries. We describe a case of undiagnosed left coronary ostial obstruction in a teenager which may have contributed to perioperative ventricular dysfunction and subsequent mortality following a reoperation many years after arterial switch.</AbstractText>
